h the primary supplier, shipping to HQ. Everything is in one order and all of it is new equipment:\n\n| SKU | Item | Qty | Unit price | Amount |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| DK-200 | USB-C Dock | 3 | $189 | $567 |\n| MN-27 | 27-inch 4K Monitor | 3 | $329 | $987 |\n| | | | **Total** | **$1,554** |\n\n- **Dock model:** DK-200 was in stock, so I didn't need the DK-210 successor. I also skipped the cheaper refurbished version (DK-200-R).\n- **Approval:** At $1,554 the order is under the $2,500 limit, so it didn't need manager approval.\n- **Problem along the way:** My first attempt timed out after only the docks line had gone through, which created a partial order (PO0001, $567). I cancelled it and the $567 was refunded. Then I resubmitted the full order using the same order key so nothing would be ordered twice. The order list now shows PO0001 as cancelled and PO0002 as the only active order, so you've been charged once, for the $1,554 total.", "type": "text"}]}]}